Chapter: SceneLimitsSpec
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter ListUtils
  cites Safari chapter SceneLimits
  cites Judge chapter Grade

 SceneLimits: three shared culls, pinned.

 THE SMALLEST SPEC IN THE SUITE, AND IT IS NOT A TAUTOLOGY. The chapter is three
 Real constants and no code, so there is no behaviour to derive and the wants are
 the numbers themselves. What the file buys is that the chapter is COMPILED AND
 LOADED by something -- a chapter with no callers in the bundle under test is
 never put through the front end at all, and the failures this suite exists to
 catch are a chapter that will not compile or syntax an arm does not accept.

 It also pins the numbers, which is worth a line each: all three are read by more
 than one population, which is the whole reason they live here rather than beside
 the population that uses them, and a change to any of them moves several
 chapters at once.

 We say:

Section: The Shared Culls

 Beyond detail-dist a tree draws as flat triangles; crown-shade-dist is the depth
 over which the crown's gradient fades to solid; scenery shorter than
 min-scenery-px on screen is skipped.

  culls-got : List Real
  culls-got = [detail-dist, crown-shade-dist, min-scenery-px]

  culls-want : List Real
  culls-want = [200.0, 80.0, 2.0]

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "sl-cull" culls-got culls-want 0.0)
  end
